Maps Stamp art: what it derives from
=========================================

Some of the built-in Maps Stamps derive from the art of Azgaar's Fantasy Map
Generator (https://github.com/Azgaar/Fantasy-Map-Generator), which is MIT
licensed. Its license text, with its copyright line, follows below. The
derived Stamps, and the source file each one was converted from, are:

- capital: src/assets/icons/burgs/illustrated/nordic-capital.svg
- city: src/assets/icons/burgs/illustrated/nordic-city.svg
- castle: src/assets/icons/burgs/illustrated/castle.svg
- temple: src/assets/icons/burgs/illustrated/greek-temple.svg
- volcano: src/assets/icons/relief/illustrated/vulcan-1.svg
- mountain: src/assets/icons/relief/illustrated/mount-1.svg
- tree: src/assets/icons/relief/illustrated/deciduous-1.svg (one tree of three)
- port: src/assets/icons/ports/anchor.svg (redrawn one-colour)
- marker: src/assets/icons/burgs/atlas/circled.svg (redrawn one-colour)

The compass-rose Stamp derives from
src/assets/icons/charges/conventional/compassRose.svg, whose own <metadata>
dedicates it to the public domain under CC0
(https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).

The remaining Stamps (town, village, ruin, tower, cave, bridge, battle,
cartouche, border-frame, sea-monster, ship) are original to Maibuk, drawn
in-house for this Plugin under the Plugin's license.

